{"body":"## Summary

Use [CodeMirror 5](https://codemirror.net/5/) with Styra's [`codemirror-rego`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/codemirror-rego) package for all Rego source rendering in the Policy Management UI — the create/edit dialog, the policy detail read-only view, and the version diff view.

## Why CodeMirror 5, not Monaco

The OPA Rego Playground (play.openpolicyagent.org) uses CodeMirror 5 with `codemirror-rego`. This is the only editor with a production-ready, maintained Rego language mode. There is no Monaco Rego package on npm (see `docs/research/rego-playground-editor-analysis.md`).

| | Monaco | CodeMirror 5 + `codemirror-rego` |
|---|---|---|
| Rego support | Custom tokenizer (~150 lines, we maintain) | Drop-in npm package (Styra maintains) |
| Bundle size | ~2MB | ~400KB |
| React wrapper | `@monaco-editor/react` | `react-codemirror2` |
| Diff view | Built-in | `merge` addon or separate lib |

CodeMirror 5 wins on effort (zero tokenizer work), correctness (Styra's mode handles the full Rego grammar), and bundle size.

## Where CodeMirror is used

| Location | Mode | Configuration |
|---|---|---|
| Create Policy dialog | Editable | `mode: "rego"`, line numbers, bracket matching |
| Policy detail page | Read-only | `mode: "rego"`, `readOnly: true` |
| Version diff view | Merge | CodeMirror `merge` addon or text diff component |
| Test panel mock input | Editable | `mode: "application/json"` (built-in) |

## Setup

```typescript
import { Controlled as CodeMirror } from "react-codemirror2";
import "codemirror/lib/codemirror.css";
import "codemirror-rego";

<CodeMirror
  value={regoSource}
  options={{
    mode: "rego",
    lineNumbers: true,
    matchBrackets: true,
    theme: "default", // or custom theme
  }}
  onBeforeChange={(editor, data, value) => setRegoSource(value)}
/>
```

## Compilation error gutter markers

When the admin clicks "Validate" and Regorus returns compilation errors with line/column, use CodeMirror's gutter and line widget APIs:

```typescript
// Clear previous markers
editor.clearGutter("error-gutter");

// Add error markers
errors.forEach(err => {
  const marker = document.createElement("div");
  marker.className = "error-marker";
  marker.title = err.message;
  editor.setGutterMarker(err.line - 1, "error-gutter", marker);
});
```

## Dependencies

- `codemirror` ^5.48.0 (peer dep of codemirror-rego)
- `codemirror-rego` (Styra, Apache-2.0)
- `react-codemirror2` (React wrapper for CodeMirror 5)
- Regorus policy evaluation engine (#194) — Rego source storage and compilation validation

## Considerations

- CodeMirror 5 is in maintenance mode (CodeMirror 6 is current). Acceptable because `codemirror-rego` only supports CM5 and there is no CM6 Rego mode. If a CM6 Rego mode appears, migration is straightforward.
- For version diff view, evaluate CodeMirror's `merge` addon vs a lightweight text diff component. The merge addon adds ~20KB.","title":"Use CodeMirror 5 with codemirror-rego for Rego source authoring and display"}

